//// rakun-starter-actuator — a starter: a curated dependency set, and no code.
////
//// Declaring it pulls `rakun-starter` and `rakun-actuator` (health, info, the endpoint host); `rakun-metrics` joins when front 75 lands it. An application keeps importing from the modules
//// themselves (`from "rakun-web"`, `from "rakun-cache"`, …); nothing is
//// importable from the starter, so a starter can drop a module without
//// breaking an import. The versions are `rakun/version_set`'s.
